---
source: crates/daemon/tests/cli_help.rs
expression: stdout
---
What needs you, not what arrived: replies you owe, promises coming due, threads waiting on someone, and new mail from people, each with the reason it is there. Everything else is summarised as counts

Usage: mxr desk [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  dismiss  Done waiting: take conversations you wrote last off Waiting on until a new message arrives in them
  restore  Undo a dismissal: the conversations wait again
  done     Done: nothing for you to do here, put it away
  later    Reply later, or wait for a reply, until a time
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --account <ACCOUNT>  Limit to one account; the default covers every account
      --limit <LIMIT>      Rows to show per lane; each lane still reports its total [default: 25]
      --gists              Show what each conversation is about and what it asks of you, where a model has already written it. Never waits on a model; `mxr briefing gists --generate` queues the missing ones
      --format <FORMAT>    [possible values: table, json, jsonl, csv, ids]
  -h, --help               Print help
